## ENTITY MODEL — SMARTSCAPE-NATIVE (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

`classicEntitySelector()` is explicitly deprecated. The four sub-skills use zero
`dt.entity.*` references. dt-rcf MUST use the Smartscape model throughout.

### Span / Log / Event Filtering

```dql
-- Filter spans to a specific service (use Smartscape, NOT dt.entity.service ==)
fetch spans
| filter dt.smartscape.service in [
    smartscapeNodes SERVICE
    | filter id == "{SERVICE_ENTITY_ID}"
    | fields id
]

-- Filter logs to a specific service
fetch logs
| filter dt.smartscape_source.id in [
    smartscapeNodes SERVICE
    | filter id == "{SERVICE_ENTITY_ID}"
    | fields id
]

-- Filter events to a specific host
fetch events
| filter dt.smartscape_source.id in [
    smartscapeNodes HOST
    | filter id == "{HOST_ENTITY_ID}"
    | fields id
]
```

### Entity Name & Metadata Resolution

```dql
-- Resolve service name on spans (preferred over fetch dt.entity.service)
fetch spans
| fieldsAdd service_name = getNodeName(dt.smartscape.service)

-- Resolve host name + hardware on spans
fetch spans
| fieldsAdd host_name = getNodeName(dt.smartscape.host),
            getNodeField(dt.smartscape.host, "bitness"),
            getNodeField(dt.smartscape.host, "additionalSystemInfo")

-- Look up host metadata directly
smartscapeNodes HOST
| filter id == "{HOST_ENTITY_ID}"
| fields name, properties

-- Look up service metadata directly
smartscapeNodes SERVICE
| filter id == "{SERVICE_ENTITY_ID}"
| fields name, properties
```

### Timeseries Metrics (JVM / Process)

```dql
-- Group by Smartscape process node (per java.md). To SCOPE to one process, filter the PGI
-- metric dimension (dt.entity.process_group_instance) — NOT dt.process_group.id, which is
-- frequently EMPTY on these series and yields false 0-row results.
timeseries gc_count = avg(dt.runtime.jvm.gc.collection_count),
           by: {dt.smartscape.process, dt.entity.process_group_instance}
| filter dt.entity.process_group_instance == "{ROOT_PGI}"
```

### Process Group Metadata (Legacy Gap)

`fetch dt.entity.process_group` has no Smartscape equivalent for `softwareTechnologies`
and `COMMAND_LINE_ARGS` metadata. Use it only for this specific purpose and document
it in the report as a legacy query:

```dql
-- LEGACY — only for softwareTechnologies/command-line metadata (no Smartscape equivalent)
fetch dt.entity.process_group
| filter id == "{PROCESS_GROUP_ID}"
| fieldsAdd entity.name, metadata, tags, softwareTechnologies
```

### Problem Correlation (Dual Model — Transition Period)

Both `affected_entity_ids` (classic) and `smartscape.affected_entity.ids` (Smartscape)
coexist on problem records. Always query BOTH with OR logic:

```dql
fetch logs, from:now() - 2h
| filter dt.smartscape_source.id in [
    fetch dt.davis.problems
    | filter display_id == "{PROBLEM_ID}"
    | filter not(dt.davis.is_duplicate)
    | fields smartscape.affected_entity.ids
] or dt.source_entity in [
    fetch dt.davis.problems
    | filter display_id == "{PROBLEM_ID}"
    | filter not(dt.davis.is_duplicate)
    | fields affected_entity_ids
]
```

### Topology Diagrams

Topology MUST be built from Smartscape relationships, not by stitching `fetch dt.entity.*`
records:

```dql
-- Service dependency topology: services this entity calls and is called by
fetch spans
| filter dt.smartscape.service in [smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id]
| filter span.kind == "client"
| fieldsAdd caller = getNodeName(dt.smartscape.service),
            callee = server.address
| summarize call_count = count(), avg_duration = avg(duration),
            by: {caller, callee}
| sort call_count desc
```

