## EXECUTION PROTOCOL

### Run logging (async, non-blocking — set up at the very start)

Maintain a per-run timing log so every run leaves diagnosable phase timing behind. Set
`LOG="RCF_{ANCHOR_SLUG}_{DATE}.log"` (next to the report) and at each phase boundary append ONE
line, **backgrounded so it never gates execution**:
```bash
{ printf '[%s] %s\n' "$(date -u +%FT%TZ)" "Phase X — <one-line summary>" >> "$LOG"; } &
```
Log: START, Phase 0b complete (DispatchContext summary), the chosen execution path
(direct vs subagent + BLAST_RADIUS), Phase 1 complete (per-worker/per-batch one-liners),
Absence-Gate result, report written, RUN COMPLETE. Phase 7 prints the log path.

