### Phase 0b: Context Bootstrap (Sequential — Orchestrator)

Build the **DispatchContext** that all phase workers receive.

**MINIMAL BOOTSTRAP — 2 queries, not 12.** Bootstrap is the orchestrator's only serial stretch,
so keep it tiny: (Q1) problem details, (Q2) the combined ROOT_PGI + k8s + runtime span query
below. Do NOT run a separate `smartscapeNodes … | fields name` lookup per affected service
(serial + flaky); resolve affected-service names in ONE batched query
(`smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "A" or id == "B" or id == "C" | fields id, name`) or
lazily via `getNodeName(dt.smartscape.service)` in the topology query. Do NOT run the
`dt.entity.process_group … softwareTechnologies` metadata query unless RUNTIME is still unknown
after Q2 (it failed twice on `entityName(...)` last run and runtime is usually obvious from the
PGI name/tags).

#### If ANCHOR_TYPE == PROBLEM

Run the dt-rca Tier 0 queries (Steps 1.1, 1.1b, 1.1c) from
`~/.claude/skills/dt-rca/SKILL.md`. Extract:

```
PROBLEM_ID            display_id from dt.davis.problems
PROBLEM_START         event.start
PROBLEM_END           event.end (null if still ACTIVE)
ROOT_ENTITY_ID        root_cause_entity_id (classic format: SERVICE-XXXX or PGI-XXXX)
ROOT_ENTITY_NAME      root_cause_entity_name
AFFECTED_ENTITY_IDS[] affected_entity_ids array
ROOT_SERVICE_ID       resolved SERVICE entity ID (from Step 1.1b)
ROOT_PGI              process group instance of the root service (resolved by the explicit
                      ROOT_PGI query below) — W-services scopes runtime metrics by this
ENTITY_TYPE           SERVICE | PGI | HOST | CUSTOM_DEVICE
INVESTIGATION_STRATEGY error | performance | resource | availability
ENTITY_TAGS[]         tags array
IS_K8S_WORKLOAD       bool (true if k8s tags present)
K8S_NAMESPACE         k8s namespace of the root workload (from entity tags / cloud_application)
K8S_WORKLOAD          k8s workload/container name (W-logs fallback filter). Often == the service
                      short name (e.g. "payment"); confirm from k8s metadata when available.
RUNTIME               java | nodejs | dotnet | python | php | go | unknown
                      (from softwareTechnologies in ENTITY_TAGS or process group)
```

**REQUIRED:** Apply `not(dt.davis.is_duplicate)` on ALL `fetch dt.davis.problems` queries.

DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW:
```
from: PROBLEM_START minus 2h
to:   PROBLEM_END plus 1h (or now() if still ACTIVE)
```

**Q2 — combined ROOT_PGI + k8s + runtime (ONE query — REQUIRED, validated 2026-05-21).** After
ROOT_SERVICE_ID is known, this single span query resolves ROOT_PGI, K8S_NAMESPACE, K8S_WORKLOAD
and the runtime hint at once — no separate name/metadata queries:
```dql
fetch spans, from:now()-{SCAN_DAYS}d
| filter dt.smartscape.service in [smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id]
| summarize spancount = count(),
            by: { dt.entity.process_group_instance, k8s.namespace.name, k8s.workload.name }
| sort spancount desc
| limit 1
```
Set `ROOT_PGI` = `dt.entity.process_group_instance` (e.g. `PROCESS_GROUP_INSTANCE-07A6B7568FB9955B`;
NEVER a `PROCESS_GROUP-…` group id), `K8S_NAMESPACE` / `K8S_WORKLOAD` from the row. RUNTIME is
usually evident from the PGI detected name (e.g. "index.js payment-*" → nodejs) or ENTITY_TAGS;
only run the legacy `dt.entity.process_group` metadata query if it's still unknown.
If Q2 returns null PGI, leave ROOT_PGI null — W-services groups runtime metrics by process and
selects the row whose `getNodeName(dt.smartscape.process)` matches ROOT_ENTITY_NAME.

